WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.257
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book two.

2
00:00:05.557 --> 00:00:09.559
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.859 --> 00:00:15.321
Unit twenty-four: Planning a Trip. Today you will talk about travel plans with going to.

4
00:00:15.621 --> 00:00:18.389
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.333 --> 00:00:22.322
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.183 --> 00:00:23.813
Trip.

7
00:00:24.817 --> 00:00:27.014
Trip means a journey to a place and back.

8
00:00:27.617 --> 00:00:29.523
We're taking a trip to the beach.

9
00:00:30.117 --> 00:00:32.223
Your turn. Say: Trip.

10
00:00:35.067 --> 00:00:35.673
Trip.

11
00:00:36.417 --> 00:00:37.522
Destination.

12
00:00:38.517 --> 00:00:41.097
Destination means the place you are travelling to.

13
00:00:41.683 --> 00:00:43.834
Our destination is Kampot.

14
00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:46.928
Your turn. Say: Destination.

15
00:00:49.767 --> 00:00:50.988
Destination.

16
00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:52.519
Budget.

17
00:00:53.517 --> 00:00:55.876
Budget means the money you plan to spend.

18
00:00:56.483 --> 00:00:58.657
Our budget is one hundred dollars.

19
00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:01.740
Your turn. Say: Budget.

20
00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:05.508
Budget.

21
00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:06.984
Ticket.

22
00:01:07.983 --> 00:01:10.691
Ticket means a paper or code that lets you travel.

23
00:01:11.283 --> 00:01:13.492
I bought two bus tickets online.

24
00:01:14.083 --> 00:01:16.469
Your turn. Say: Ticket.

25
00:01:19.333 --> 00:01:20.242
Ticket.

26
00:01:20.983 --> 00:01:21.880
Hotel.

27
00:01:22.883 --> 00:01:25.893
Hotel means a building where travellers pay to stay.

28
00:01:26.483 --> 00:01:28.169
The hotel is near the river.

29
00:01:28.783 --> 00:01:31.598
Your turn. Say: Hotel.

30
00:01:34.433 --> 00:01:35.434
Hotel.

31
00:01:36.183 --> 00:01:36.848
Pack.

32
00:01:37.850 --> 00:01:40.233
Pack means to put things in a bag for a trip.

33
00:01:40.817 --> 00:01:42.317
I'm going to pack tonight.

34
00:01:42.917 --> 00:01:45.163
Your turn. Say: Pack.

35
00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:48.711
Pack.

36
00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:50.672
Itinerary.

37
00:01:51.683 --> 00:01:55.088
Itinerary means a plan of a journey with places and times.

38
00:01:55.683 --> 00:01:58.182
Our itinerary includes Bokor Mountain.

39
00:01:58.783 --> 00:02:01.482
Your turn. Say: Itinerary.

40
00:02:04.333 --> 00:02:05.520
Itinerary.

41
00:02:06.283 --> 00:02:07.041
Map.

42
00:02:08.050 --> 00:02:10.827
Map means a picture that shows places and roads.

43
00:02:11.417 --> 00:02:13.033
Check the map before you go.

44
00:02:13.617 --> 00:02:15.990
Your turn. Say: Map.

45
00:02:18.833 --> 00:02:19.625
Map.

46
00:02:20.433 --> 00:02:24.502
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:25.350 --> 00:02:27.559
Visal, where are you going for the holiday?

48
00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:30.464
We're going to visit Kampot!

49
00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:33.201
Have you planned everything?

50
00:02:34.317 --> 00:02:40.313
Yes. We have a budget, and my dad booked the tickets and the hotel.

51
00:02:41.417 --> 00:02:42.871
What are you going to do there?

52
00:02:43.983 --> 00:02:47.785
We're going to climb Bokor Mountain. I'm going to pack tonight!

53
00:02:48.933 --> 00:02:50.736
Part three: grammar.

54
00:02:51.583 --> 00:02:54.047
Grammar focus: Going to (plans).

55
00:02:54.347 --> 00:02:55.511
Look at the pattern.

56
00:02:56.217 --> 00:02:57.949
We're going to visit Kampot.

57
00:02:58.850 --> 00:03:00.246
I'm going to pack tonight.

58
00:03:01.150 --> 00:03:02.987
Is she going to book the hotel?

59
00:03:03.933 --> 00:03:06.420
Use 'going to' for plans you decided before now.

60
00:03:07.183 --> 00:03:10.962
Be careful! Don't say: We going to visit Kampot.

61
00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:15.422
Say: We're going to visit Kampot.

62
00:03:15.722 --> 00:03:18.163
Don't forget am, is or are before 'going to'.

63
00:03:18.967 --> 00:03:21.573
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:22.367 --> 00:03:23.879
Our Kampot Trip.

65
00:03:24.179 --> 00:03:25.888
Planning a trip takes time.

66
00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:29.747
First, we chose a destination and set a budget.

67
00:03:30.733 --> 00:03:34.358
Next, we booked a ticket and a hotel, and made an itinerary.

68
00:03:35.367 --> 00:03:38.179
We are going to check the map and visit the pepper farms.

69
00:03:39.167 --> 00:03:42.095
Tonight, I'm going to pack the right clothes for the mountain.

70
00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:47.144
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

71
00:03:47.983 --> 00:03:50.134
We blank going to visit Kampot.

72
00:03:50.434 --> 00:03:53.251
A, are. B, is. C, will.

73
00:03:56.800 --> 00:03:58.533
The answer is A: are.

74
00:03:59.683 --> 00:04:01.811
The money you plan to spend is your blank.

75
00:04:02.111 --> 00:04:05.497
A, budget. B, ticket. C, map.

76
00:04:09.033 --> 00:04:10.673
The answer is A: budget.

77
00:04:11.817 --> 00:04:14.281
To put things in a bag for a trip is to blank.

78
00:04:14.581 --> 00:04:17.897
A, pack. B, plan. C, book.

79
00:04:21.433 --> 00:04:23.259
The answer is A: pack.

80
00:04:24.467 --> 00:04:27.444
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

81
00:04:28.283 --> 00:04:30.573
Where would you like to go on your next trip?

82
00:04:39.383 --> 00:04:40.988
Now listen to Visal.

83
00:04:41.288 --> 00:04:47.609
I'd like to go to Siem Reap. We're going to visit Angkor Wat at sunrise, and I'm going to take lots of photos.

84
00:04:47.909 --> 00:04:49.642
Excellent answer, Visal!

85
00:04:50.550 --> 00:04:54.317
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and going to (plans).

86
00:04:54.617 --> 00:04:59.289
Today's value is planning ahead. Make a plan and take small steps every day.

87
00:04:59.589 --> 00:05:02.567
See you in Unit twenty-five. Goodbye!

88
00:05:02.867 --> 00:05:05.809
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

